'' A temporary string key for 'operator []( byref k as string )' is copied before the
'' call, as an ordinary call's byref string argument is: concatenations, str( ), a
'' literal, compound and plain read-modify-write. tiko passed the temporary itself, so
'' updates were lost, a str( ) key came out empty, and 't[ k ] = t[ k ] + 1' freed the
'' buffer twice. Expected output is fbc-modern 1.20's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/udt-index-temp-key.bas -o tests/codegen/udtindextempkey.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/udtindextempkey.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [a] 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [b] 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [7] 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [c] 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [d1] 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [d0] 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [e] 0
